  "name": "Fire Release: Heated Sun",
  "type": "jutsu",
  "img": "icons/svg/book.svg",
  "system": {
    "identifier": "fire-release-heated-sun",
    "description": "<p>You create a globe of white-hot Fire on a point you select within range, that you can see. Creatures who begin their turns within 20 feet of the Globe must make a constitution saving throw, gaining two ranks of Weakened on a failed save. Flammable objects within 20 feet of it ignite, and metal begins to become too hot to touch causing those wearing or holding metal within range to take 6d6+6 Fire damage at the beginning of each turn they are in contact with it.</p>\n<p>As an action, you may move this globe 30 feet in any direction from its current placement.</p>\n<p>At Higher Ranks: For each rank you cast this jutsu above B-Rank, increase the cost of this jutsu by 3 and increase damage by 1d6+1.</p>",
